(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase468IntentGoalPracticeLifecycle"
  :createdAt 1789292000000
  :status "completed"
  :priorityOrder 3
  :summary "Intent, Goal and Practice Lifecycle: three kinds distinguished by what closes them, a stated threshold for writing, a retirement path that is actually used, and a state view that can be read later."
  :phase "Phase468IntentGoalPracticeLifecycle"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-12. Project memory totals 469582 tokens: 283902 across 77 task files, 73784 across 62 decision files, 86185 in eleven top level ledgers, 24802 in seven reviews. Nothing retires. Across every top level ledger the status distribution is 86 active, 66 verified, 8 settled, 3 planned and exactly 1 superseded, so of 164 status bearing records one has ever been withdrawn. intent.asn holds 89 intents and not one carries a status field at all. practices.asn holds 10 practices and all 10 are active. No document anywhere states when an agent may add an intent, a goal or a practice, so the threshold is whatever the writing agent felt at the time. The one automated view, asl audit consistency, reports 39 phases from a literal in the source while the roadmap holds 58."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task46801" :parentId "" :phase "phase-468"
      :title "Three kinds, distinguished by what closes them"
      :kind :protocol :state :completed :lane "model" :priority :critical :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789292000000 :updatedAt 1789292000000
      :motivation "Intents, goals and practices are currently three words for one thing: a durable record that is written and never revisited. Ninety nine records across two ledgers carry between them one status field family and no closure condition. Without a closure condition a record cannot be wrong, cannot be finished and cannot be removed, so the store can only grow, and it has: 469582 tokens."
      :purpose "Each kind is defined by what ends it, which is the only definition that produces a lifecycle. An intent is why the work is being done and it closes when the reason no longer holds, which is a judgement an agent may make with evidence. A goal is what done looks like and it closes when the stated observable is true, which is decidable. A practice is how the work is done and it closes when it stops being followed or when a measurement contradicts it. Every record carries its closure condition at creation, and a record whose closure condition cannot be evaluated is not accepted."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Three kinds defined by closure, not by topic" "A closure condition mandatory at creation" "An unevaluable closure condition rejected" "Growth becomes bounded by construction"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/intent.asn" ".asl/mem/practices.asn" "mem/src/records.asl"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "concepts" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D46" "D52" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46801"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46801.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A goal whose observable is already true is closed by evaluation, not by hand." "A record without a closure condition is refused at creation." "A closure condition that no command can evaluate is refused."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46801" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46801-verified-20260912"] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the three closures." "Require the condition." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts ["rc-task46801-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46802" :parentId "" :phase "phase-468"
      :title "The threshold for writing: would the next agent regret its absence"
      :kind :protocol :state :completed :lane "model" :priority :critical :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789292000000 :updatedAt 1789292000000
      :motivation "Nothing states when an agent should write a durable record, so 89 intents accumulated under no threshold at all. A checklist would be the wrong correction: it would produce records to satisfy the checklist, which is how a store becomes a dump while looking diligent. What is needed is a test an intelligent agent can apply to a specific situation."
      :purpose "One test governs writing: would an agent arriving later, without this session, be unable to reconstruct this from the tree. Anything reconstructible from the code, the history or a command is not written down, because it is already recorded where it belongs. What survives that test is the small set the store exists for: a reason that leaves no trace, a constraint that came from outside, a decision between options where the rejected ones matter, a measurement that was expensive to obtain. The test is stated as a reason and not as a form, so an agent applies judgement rather than filling fields."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One reconstructibility test governing every write" "Reconstructible content refused rather than duplicated" "Judgement preserved, no checklist" "The store holds what cannot be recovered otherwise"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/rules.asn" ".asl/mem/principles.asn"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "budget" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46801" "Task46504"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46802"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46802.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A record restating what a command already reports is refused, and the refusal names the command." "A record of a rejected alternative is accepted, since no command reports what was not chosen." "The test is applied by the writing agent and the check does not enumerate acceptable topics."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46802" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46802-verified-20260912"] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["State the test." "Check reconstructibility mechanically where possible." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts ["rc-task46802-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46803" :parentId "" :phase "phase-468"
      :title "Retirement that is used, not merely available"
      :kind :remediation :state :completed :lane "lifecycle" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789292000000 :updatedAt 1789292000000
      :motivation "A superseded status exists and has been applied once in the history of the repository, against 86 active and 66 verified records. A retirement path that is available and unused is the same as no retirement path, and the evidence that it is unused is the 469582 token store. The existing machinery for this is already written and passing: amnesia implements deliberate forgetting and context scoring implements eviction of what is not referenced."
      :purpose "Closure conditions are evaluated on a schedule rather than on memory, and a record whose condition is met is retired with what it produced preserved. Retirement is a transition and not a deletion: the record moves to a closed set that is not loaded but is queryable, so nothing is lost and nothing unnecessary is carried. The volume of the active set is reported, so the store cannot grow unnoticed again."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Closure conditions evaluated rather than remembered" "Retirement preserves the product and drops the carrying cost" "Active set volume reported" "The existing amnesia and scoring modules given a caller"]
      :owns [".asl/mem" "mem/src/amnesia.asl" "mem/src/context_scoring.asl"]
      :targetSymbols ["evict-below-threshold" "penalize-unreferenced-matches"] :relatedSymbols ["budget" "capabilities"]
      :invariants ["D46" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46801" "Task46503"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46803"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46803.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A record whose closure condition becomes true is retired by the next evaluation without a hand edit." "A retired record is still queryable and is not loaded." "The active set volume is reported and a growth beyond the stated bound fails."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46803" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46803-verified-20260912"] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Evaluate conditions on a schedule." "Move rather than delete." "Report volume." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts ["rc-task46803-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46804" :parentId "" :phase "phase-468"
      :title "A state view that is computed, so it can be trusted later"
      :kind :tooling :state :completed :lane "observability" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789292000000 :updatedAt 1789292000000
      :motivation "The single automated view of project state reports 39 phases from a literal in the source while the roadmap holds 58, and reports zero discrepancies while doing so. A view that is wrong is worse than no view, because it is consulted instead of looking. Observability that cannot be trusted is the reason the certification failure in this repository went unnoticed."
      :purpose "One view answers what is open, what closed and when, what is blocked and on what, and what changed since a given point, computed from the ledgers every time rather than held anywhere. Every number it prints is a computed value. It is bounded and continuable, since the store is 469582 tokens and a view that returns all of it is not a view."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Open, closed, blocked and changed-since, all computed" "No literal in any reported number" "Bounded and continuable output" "The 39 against 58 discrepancy resolved"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_audit_consistency" "phase_count"] :relatedSymbols ["output" "anchor" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D52" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task45504" "Task46801"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46804"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46804.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Adding a phase changes the reported count." "Every number in the output changes when the thing it counts changes." "A changed-since query returns only what changed after the given point."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46804" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46804-verified-20260912"] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Compute every reported number." "Add changed-since." "Bound the output." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts ["rc-task46804-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46805" :parentId "" :phase "phase-468"
      :title "One surface over intents, goals, practices and notes"
      :kind :tooling :state :completed :lane "observability" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789292000000 :updatedAt 1789292000000
      :motivation "Intents, goals, practices and notes are four stores with four shapes, no common way to write and no common way to read, and an agent reaches them by editing files. The memory package already provides records, retrieval and promotion; what is missing is one way in and one way out."
      :purpose "One surface writes and reads all four, distinguishing them by their closure condition rather than by a separate command each. Writing is cheap enough that an agent does it while working rather than at the end. Retrieval is by query over the existing BM25 index rather than by path, so a record is found without knowing where it was put, and promotion between kinds uses the path that already exists."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One surface for four stores" "Query retrieval rather than path retrieval" "Writing cheap enough to be done while working" "Promotion between kinds through the existing path"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "mem/src/notes.asl" "mem/src/spool_search.asl" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["note-promote-to-task" "note-promote-to-adr" "spool-query-bm25"] :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "capabilities" "tools"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46501" "Task46801"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46805"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46805.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A record written as one kind and promoted to another keeps its history." "A query finds a record without its path being known." "The surface writes to the same files a hand edit would, so nothing is stored twice."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46805" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46805-verified-20260912"] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Unify the write path." "Retrieve by query." "Wire promotion." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts ["rc-task46805-verified-20260912"])]
  :notes "The measured problem is not disorganisation but the absence of an ending. One record in the repository's history has ever been superseded, and the store is 469582 tokens. Defining each kind by what closes it is what makes every other part of this phase possible.")
